WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:04.256
Unit eight. Basic Email Concepts!

2
00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:10.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.365 --> 00:00:13.632
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.682 --> 00:00:18.048
Today we learn about Basic Email Concepts. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:23.395
Email. Say it with me. Email!

6
00:00:26.904 --> 00:00:31.104
Inbox. Say it with me. Inbox!

7
00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:38.237
Sender. Say it with me. Sender!

8
00:00:41.785 --> 00:00:46.018
Recipient. Say it with me. Recipient!

9
00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:54.017
Subject line. Say it with me. Subject line!

10
00:00:57.573 --> 00:01:01.404
Message. Say it with me. Message!

11
00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:08.448
Send. Say it with me. Send!

12
00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:16.107
Reply. Say it with me. Reply!

13
00:01:19.602 --> 00:01:29.233
Email is a way to send a message to a recipient. I write a subject line and message, then send it. The sender's inbox shows a reply.

14
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:32.985
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:33.962 --> 00:01:39.391
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:39.441 --> 00:01:40.591
Sender!

17
00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:47.321
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:47.371 --> 00:01:48.521
Send!

19
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:58.190
Did you know? The first email was sent in 1971, long before most people even had a home computer!

20
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.298
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:12.823
Think and answer. What is one reason someone might use email instead of a text message?

22
00:02:12.873 --> 00:02:14.079
Great answer!

23
00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:21.157
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.267
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

